HST Office: Word Find loops end, and Font.Color and ColorIndex give Word's colors.

- While .Execute on a Range never ended: each search started again at the top of the found text. As in
  Word, a range the search redefined, or a collapsed one, now searches on from its end; other ranges
  are searched inside. This hung the office on testFontColor, and is how Word macros walk a document.
- Font.Color is BGR in Word (wdColorRed = 255) but went to CharColor unconverted, so red text came out
  blue. Font.ColorIndex used Excel's palette and failed on wdAuto; it now has WdColorIndex's values.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/vba-corpus/regression_cases.py (FindLoop*, FontColor*); upstream testFontColor.docm.
